WEBVTT

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:18.210
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.750
Kumo to kumo amime o nukete

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.290
Odoru hane kaze o matou

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.750
Me no mae de hoshi ga ochiteiku

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:39.040
Akogareta aoi ao

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.080
Nijimu chihyou keriageta

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:47.290
Kikasete yo kimi dake no sora no ne o

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:56.630
Tobidatsu jyuuryoku o mikata ni tsukete

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:03.040
Mou ichido nando demo warai nagara

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:10.080
Bokura wa ushiro o muite tobou to wa shinai

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:15.290
Tsukinai yume asu o otte ikiru

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.790
Waita zetsubou ni ai o tozashita

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:21.080
Yowai boku wa kirai da

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:27.040
Nagareru ima mukau saki wa mirai

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:35.960
Elite Fortress

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:36.750
Fly forth, KOTOBUKI Corps!

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:40.000
Tomorrow is the day we have waited for!

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:43.880
Now one pancake! Two pancakes!
Three and four and five pancakes!

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:48.330
Yes we, we are the KOTOBUKI-

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:50.580
Enough of your tone-deaf nonsense already!

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.830
Nothing can stop a good song once it starts!

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:56.040
Plus, squeezing you aboard has already
thrown my fuel efficiency into a nosedive.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.460
Don't make it worse by complaining!

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:57.710
A nosedive?

00:01:57.830 --> 00:01:59.580
I don't weigh that much, you know!

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:01.040
You weigh how many pounds, again?

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:02.330
It's not by choice.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:05.500
Unlike you I merely have a 
more full figure, is all.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.170
Don't forget, this is all because you went
and got shot down yourself!

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:23.920
Our wings are rays of light!

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.040
Stop-!

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.540
Kylie!

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:32.880
Settle down, Kylie!

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.710
One of my flaps was feeling a little stuck
so I'm just trying to shake it loose!

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:37.250
That's not fair, Kylie!

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.580
Reona, my right flap feels off, too!

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:40.580
And my rudder seems rather tight.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.460
These girls...

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:51.500
Where's the harm in it?

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.380
I won't pretend I don't feel the same way.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:56.830
We haven't had any time to 
fly off the clock in a while.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:00.790
Technically we're still "on the clock"
until we get that Raiden back.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:04.750
Still, it's been a good while since we've taken
our Hayabusas out for such a long flight.

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:09.130
We need to fly free like 
that every now and again.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.460
To remind ourselves how 
free the great blue sky is.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.750
And that we only get to fly through it
because of that freedom.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.670
Freedom doesn't come cheap, though.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:18.290
And that's what makes it precious.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:19.170
Now then!

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:20.210
Zara!

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.250
Sheesh...

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:41.540
What's your problem, cargo gal?

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.380
Well...

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.250
Will it still be a ways 
to the Roota Airfield?

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:47.250
Huh, I dunno. Why?

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:51.210
N-no reason. Just...

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:56.330
Well pardon me, girls,
but Emma here needs to visit the ladies room!

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.830
Can she hold it just a bit longer?

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:02.170
We should make it in 
another ten minutes or so.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:04.000
I think she's good!

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:08.670
Roota is a great big place. 
A really lovely airfield.

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:10.000
You sure know a lot about it.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.580
Have you been out to Roota before?

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:14.750
Way back when the Corps 
was just me and Reona.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.580
It was always so lively.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.580
And always stocked up with 
plenty of vending machines.

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:20.920
Any with curry udon?!

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:21.830
There should be.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:23.170
And burgers?

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:23.830
You bet.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:24.750
What about pancakes?

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:25.290
But of course!

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:28.250
Yippee!

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.580
Curry udon!

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:46.830
I can handle this.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:47.960
Do I have your permission, Reona?

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:48.460
Sure.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.420
Hey! That's my plane you just kicked there!

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:25.080
Uhmm...

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.000
That way.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:26.830
Pardon me...

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:29.830
Hey, you old fart!

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:32.330
Is that how you greet people out here?!

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:35.790
Sorry, I thought those rascals might be back.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:39.830
The stinkin' pirates that left 
Roota in a mess like this.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:42.170
Was it Elite Industries?

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:45.080
Those morons pretending
they're running some sort of business?

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:46.540
Nah, it wasn't them.

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:49.250
It was a scarier lot than that.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:52.500
They just flew in, hit our 
main facilities, and took off.

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:54.670
What about the pancakes?

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:54.670
What about the udon?

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:54.670
What about the burgers?

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.170
Nooo!

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:05.630
No...

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:07.880
How could this be?

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:09.920
I wondered what you might be screaming about.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:11.500
This is unforgivable!

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:12.630
Unforgivable!

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:14.330
First they shoot up Rahama, 
and now my pancakes?!

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:16.880
These were two different groups, though.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:20.290
Plus, I figured we could 
all eat together here...

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:22.750
So I went ahead and packed 
enough for everyone.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:24.580
This is so good!

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:25.880
The best!

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:27.710
True bliss. Everything is delicious.

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:29.710
Is this the first time you girls have
ever had some of Zara's cooking?

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:30.170
Yep!

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:30.830
Oh yes.

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:32.960
I never would have imagined 
you had such a knack for it!

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:34.210
Thanks.

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:35.540
I picked it up a long while back.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:39.000
I used to work at an airfield like this.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.500
That's where I first met Reona, actually.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:42.830
Really?

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:43.460
I never knew.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:44.830
Which airfield?

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:45.540
Sapo.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:48.380
Sapo was tiny, but it 
sure was a good airfield.

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:49.500
It was.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:51.170
A good place indeed.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:56.670
It sounded like you knew
about Elite Industries well enough.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:00.040
We're trying to sneak into
their stronghold unnoticed, see...

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:01.790
That'll be hard to pull off.

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:04.660
They're holed up in a cave they've carved out
of this big stone mountain.

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:06.900
A real natural fortress.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:10.500
We should just fly straight in,
bust 'em up, take the Raiden and leave!

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:12.580
And what if they fly the 
Raiden out to fight us?

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:14.790
Do you wanna pull a mid-air hijack
like that boss of theirs?

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:15.670
No way!

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:17.040
Absolutely not.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.960
It would be hard to return this
if we went in guns blazing, too.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:21.170
And what might that be?

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:22.790
An "ukiyo-e," apparently...

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.580
Drawn by some young lady, it would seem.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:25.880
Their little empress, there?

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:26.750
You've met her?

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.540
Nah, but she's the girl their boss
spends all his money on.

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:34.080
The whole lot of 'em grow soft 
as kittens in her presence.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:36.080
She's gotta be nothing but bad news.

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:39.710
Well at any rate, we can't attack without
scouting the place out first.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:41.460
We need to find some way to get close.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:44.330
Well lookie here, we've got another visitor.

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:54.750
We were supposed to be performing 
for a company dinner!

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:56.630
You never said it was for 
a company of air pirates!

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:56.960
What's their deal?

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:57.750
Come on!

00:07:56.960 --> 00:07:58.670
They're a traveling tavern.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:58.670
I said no!

00:07:58.670 --> 00:07:59.960
Please!

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:03.580
Elite Industries throws these "pub"-licity events
and calls out all these gals, see.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:02.580
I'll pay you extra for it and 
everything, come on, I'm begging you!

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:02.920
No way!

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:03.750
Absolutely not!

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.040
I ain't heard nothing but bad things.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:08.170
But whaddya expect from 
a bunch of air pirates?

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:10.290
Ack, what am I gonna do?

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:13.380
These are air pirates we're dealing with,
I can't just go back on our deal now...

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:17.080
We can't put on a performance 
with numbers like these!

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:23.420
Get a load of this!

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:25.670
This is another masterpiece 
if I've ever seen one!

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:28.000
It's so cool! So incredible!

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:30.380
What about it do you find so incredible?

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:33.420
Well, you know... All of it!

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:37.570
Listen, I'm gonna make sure 
the whole world out there

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:39.660
sees just how amazing your work is!

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:40.880
That's a promise!

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:47.790
Maybe I'm no good at this after all.

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:07.170
Ladies and gents the moment you 
have all waited for is here!

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:08.830
Behold the Agua Dance Troupe!

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:11.000
They're finally here!

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:15.170
Hello there! Thank you all 
for such a lively welcome!

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:16.290
Smooch!

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:19.000
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:50.040
Well, color me surprised.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:51.380
I never imagined you could dance like that.

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:53.630
Let's just say I've got experience.

00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:58.000
It's a real work of art, eh there, new girl?

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:01.170
Now as a man of the arts I can be tough to please,


00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:03.560
but you were great out there. 
Lemme buy you a drink.

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:04.750
Be my guest!

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:06.000
Get us two lite beers!

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.670
What? I'll take a straight vodka and gin.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:10.380
Wow!

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.630
That's gotta be like 50 proof!

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:13.000
She drinks harder than the boss himself!

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.630
I'll take it straight too, then!

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:15.750
How lovely!

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:17.290
To the arts!

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:18.040
Cheers!

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:21.750
The boss can't hold his liquor like that...

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:27.580
Jeez, boss!

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:29.630
See what I mean?
He just hates to be outdone.

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:32.880
Can't anyone here hold their drink?

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:33.880
Lemme buy you a drink!

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:33.880
I can!

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:35.080
I'll buy your next round!

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:35.080
Me, me!

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:38.210
You really are something.

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:39.580
I've just got experience.

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:41.040
Now then.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:42.790
I need to fix my makeup.

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:43.920
Take your time!

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:45.000
Oh, I will!

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:51.170
Just my luck, getting stuck on shift today.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:54.130
At least we're not on guard duty.

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:06.380
The boss and the young lady are
the only ones with the keys, yes?

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:08.920
Why don't we rig it to blow, too?

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:11.540
Perhaps as a last resort.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:14.210
A broken Raiden won't do 
us much good, now will it?

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:20.380
You...!

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:22.330
Sorry for snooping.

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:25.250
I just didn't want to 
break your focus, there.

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:27.790
Are you a fan of Hokusai?

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.830
Or maybe Kunishige?

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:31.710
You know about their works?!

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:33.130
You could say I've got a bit of experience.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.750
What do you think of my art?

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:38.460
I think they might be a bit 
too on-point for ukiyo-e.

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:45.170
I get the sense that ukiyo-e are more focused
on the artist's own perception.

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:48.540
But yours are more like an exact image.

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:52.130
I think that might make 
them seem a little forced.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:56.040
I still quite like these 
works of yours, though.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:02.670
One look and I can tell how much
you really love the art you do.

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:04.210
Model!

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:06.210
Will you model for me?

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:19.880
There you are! We're here!

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:23.830
We're here to assault the 
base, stir up commotion,

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:27.440
and make it easier for Zara 
to work from the inside.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:30.710
Getting as close as we can 
without being spotted is key.

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:34.380
This all rests on how well we can work
our way through this valley.

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:35.250
Roger!

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:56.670
C'mon!

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:59.750
Here goes!

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:32.250
We're under attack!

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:38.500
Whuzzat?!

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:39.710
We're under attack!

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:41.630
They're right on top of us!

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:43.710
Yahoo!

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:45.750
Kylie and Kate, you hit those tanks.

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:47.130
Chika and I will focus on the fighters.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:48.540
Emma, you keep an eye to the skies for us.

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:50.780
If Zara doesn't show up in ten minutes, we all make


00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:52.960
emergency landings and move in to rescue her.

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:54.670
And when we do, we abandon the Raiden.

00:13:54.670 --> 00:13:55.460
Got it?

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:14.080
I've got the right side!

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:14.920
I'll take left.

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:26.040
Boss, it's the KOTOBUKI Corps!

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:28.000
Dangit! They must be after our paintings!

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:28.880
Isn't it the Raiden...?

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:30.080
It's time to send 'em home crying!

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:30.960
Suit up!

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:33.920
You know, this might just be our chance.

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:34.960
I'll handle the Raiden.

00:14:48.710 --> 00:14:49.630
Yikes!

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:50.960
Doofus.

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:51.580
Shut up!

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:55.580
Here they come!

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:20.500
Are we under attack?

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:21.880
It seems that way.

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:28.500
There's no time to waste.
Hand over the key to the Raiden.

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:29.630
No...

00:15:29.630 --> 00:15:32.040
The boss and his gang are all airborne now.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:34.080
No one's gonna come help you anymore.

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:36.170
Now hand it over.

00:16:03.130 --> 00:16:06.000
How dare you hurt my darling staff!

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:09.670
Where are you, Zara?

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:12.170
HR Chief, cover my rear!

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:15.250
Leave, I say, leave that to me.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.460
Well, that won't do.

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:25.040
You little...!

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:26.630
My apologies, sir.

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:29.410
But due to personal circumstances,

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:33.550
I am resigning from my position at 
this miserable company as of today.

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:34.710
What?! Do you think this is a joke?!

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:38.580
All of you, take down the HR Chief!

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:42.580
The HR and Sales divisions 
are all on my side.

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:44.080
And after some careful discussion...

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:49.710
We decided we would take our share of Hayabusas,
Suiseis, and the Raiden as severance!

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:55.380
Our co-conspirators should be relieving
the young lady of her key right about now.

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:59.750
You've really gone and done it now!

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:17.500
Boss?!

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:19.000
Somebody cover the boss!

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:20.960
The HR Chief is a traitor!

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:22.630
The whole Sales team, too!

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:24.210
We've got trouble!

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:26.500
I'm headed back to the 
ground, you cover for me!

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:29.670
Not if I have any say!

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.040
Was that friendly fire?!

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:32.000
They're friends no more.

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:36.290
The boss is about to get shot 
down by our pals out there.

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:38.790
It's too late now.

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:40.290
Now hand it over!

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:42.080
Yeowch!

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:46.170
You...!

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:49.290
...are way too strong.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:51.580
Who are you?

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:53.670
Zara from the KOTOBUKI Corps.

00:17:54.080 --> 00:17:56.330
I'm here to take back the Raiden.

00:17:56.330 --> 00:17:57.460
Sorry for hiding that from you.

00:17:57.460 --> 00:17:58.670
I don't care about any of that!

00:18:00.710 --> 00:18:03.040
Here's the key. Please go save him!

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:27.630
Zara!

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:29.960
Sorry I'm late. What's the situation?

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:31.210
It's a mess!

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:33.000
Whose side are we supposed to take?

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:34.630
Or are we just gonna shoot 'em all down?

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:37.460
I made a promise that we'd help out.

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:38.630
So...!

00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:42.710
The Raiden?!

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:50.920
Well, there goes everything.

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:53.290
I'll get an earful for this, but so be it.

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:56.960
We failed to obtain the Raiden. 
All craft, we're pulling out!

00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:58.420
Like hell you are!

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:02.330
So we shoot down the Suiseis?

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:05.460
Yep, they've gone and stirred 
up trouble with the boss.

00:19:05.460 --> 00:19:06.330
Roger that!

00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:12.960
Well, now. This won't do.

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:15.540
Stick to the course, we'll hold them off.

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:17.630
We'll meet at the rendezvous point!

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:26.630
Watch out for that rear gun!

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:27.380
I will!

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:33.130
We got what we came here for.

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.670
Let him go, Zara.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:37.000
Sure.

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:39.000
Welcome back.

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:41.460
Glad I made it.

00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:53.830
Sorry about all that.

00:20:54.170 --> 00:20:56.380
You can have the Raiden back. I want you to.

00:20:56.380 --> 00:20:58.540
Fine. Let's call it even here.

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:04.460
Let this be a lesson to ya to 
start working an honest job!

00:21:05.170 --> 00:21:06.750
I know, it's just...

00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:12.420
We brought this along to return it,
but do you think it's okay if I keep it?

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:14.630
I'd love you to!

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:19.210
Now if only we got to get some of
that curry udon from the vending machine!

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:20.170
Agh! I almost forgot!

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.920
I'm sure it will all be in working order
the next time we're here.

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:25.040
I do hope so.

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:26.080
So do I! So do I!

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:30.000
Honestly though, I can't stand this sluggish,
cumbersome excuse for a plane!

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:32.040
You wanna ride in the back with me again?

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:33.630
No, I will certainly abstain from such!

00:21:34.250 --> 00:21:38.130
By the time we get back to Rahama,
your Hayabusa should be good as new, Emma.

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:39.040
Just stick it out.

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:42.250
She's right. Plus, it's a 
fine plane, that Raiden.

00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:44.170
It's more equipped than the Hayabusa.

00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:45.170
And faster!

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:47.080
I'll gladly trade.

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:47.920
No, thank you.

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:48.670
Gah!

00:21:51.420 --> 00:21:53.710
We still all love our Hayabusas 
best, right, girls?

00:21:53.710 --> 00:21:54.920
'Course we do!

00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:08.580
Ano sora o jiyuu ni kakenukete mitai to

00:22:08.580 --> 00:22:12.420
Hanasaki no kaze ni negai o noseta

00:22:12.420 --> 00:22:16.330
Akogare ga keshiki o tsukutteiku

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:20.750
Ano toki no kaze wa genki kanaa

00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:29.080
Nan no tame ni tatakau no kana

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:33.130
Koko ni iru riyuu wa nan darou?

00:22:33.130 --> 00:22:41.380
Toikaketa sora wa kotaenai kedo

00:22:42.080 --> 00:22:49.040
Bokura wa tsubasa o motteiru

00:22:49.040 --> 00:22:53.750
Haruka kanata nageki no shuuchakuten

00:22:53.750 --> 00:22:58.000
Mitsuketa monogataritachi

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:05.750
Kono sora wa dare ni mo ubaenai

00:23:05.920 --> 00:23:10.460
Boku wa kakeru nanimo kowakunai yo

00:23:10.460 --> 00:23:17.630
Shiawase nara koko ni aru yo

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:27.460
Preview

00:23:33.250 --> 00:23:37.750
Next time on The Magnificent KOTOBUKI,
"The Splendid Aleshma"!

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:41.000
The Splendid Aleshma
